mpr: the provider asks for the password and shows Map Network Drive

WNetAddConnection3 with CONNECT_INTERACTIVE reaches the provider, which asks
the user for a name and password as Windows does. WNetConnectionDialog1 and
WNetDisconnectDialog are the provider's own dialogs (ntlanman.dll), and
WNetGetUniversalName gives the \\server\share of a path on a network drive.

--- a/dlls/mpr/wnet.c	2026-10-10 19:19:58.262823106 +0200
